PS5 HDMI: VRR test 10b (hdmi.vrr_test=1)                   [ps5-bazzite-deck, test only]

Decoding the stock VRR function 0x4b8b60 from hsgodd's 13.60 kernel dump
gives exactly the block test 7-9 already write (code 1, block write of 5
records: 1047=30 6064=03 600c=01,00 6c07=80 7214=80,02; with 0x35366a0==1
also 1047|=0f and 7214[1]|=01, 0 in the dump), plus 6224=40,0f in
configParamFlava3Pre. The other VRR-flag sites (0x9200, 0x3261/0x3262,
0x300a, 0x0109, 0x8000=00,01,07,80 after 0x9002) are Verde paths. So on
FLAVA3 the bridge register writes match stock, and TVs still drop the
signal ~3.5 s after the bridge enters VRR mode, even with no flips.

The remaining difference is what the GPU sends the bridge. The bridge is a
DP-to-HDMI converter; amdgpu drives a whitelisted converter (PCON) for VRR
with the VESA Adaptive-Sync SDP plus AMD's FreeSync SDP, which the
converter turns into HDMI VRR signalling. Test 10 = test 9 plus:
  - the connector is treated as a whitelisted PCON while VRR is offered
    (as_type, pack_sdp_v1_3, the sink's AMD VSDB), so amdgpu builds both SDPs,
  - vrr_sdp (default 3): bit 0 Adaptive-Sync SDP, bit 1 FreeSync SDP,
  - both only while VRR is active, and an SDP change reaches the display core
    (amdgpu only passed the FreeSync packet on as a stream update).
Opt-in with hdmi.vrr_test=1; not for a release.
10b: "ignore MSA" only while VRR is on (the bridge in VRR mode); test 10 set it
for every VRR-capable mode, and with the bridge in its normal mode that
loses the picture (no signal / blinking with VRR off, hsgodd).
